# Sprint 67 P0.1 — DONE (verified deployed)

## Goal

Sprint 67 P0.1 — personal identity (server-side persistence, ask-once)
+ Next Best Actions (deterministic resolver, portal chip UI, single
execution path). This is the actual current sprint; the stale
`.opencode/GOAL.md` describes the earlier Gmail OAuth recovery goal
that was completed in commit `686ebdb`.

## What shipped

- **P0.1-A — personal identity**: Company DNA carries
  `entrepreneurPreferredName` + `entrepreneurNameRequestedAt`
  (additive migration). `personal-identity.ts` captures names from
  explicit introductions and bare answers to the canonical question,
  persists server-side without touching business facts. Runtime
  context exposes `userPreferredName` + `userNameRequestedAt` so the
  engine uses the name sparingly and asks once.

- **P0.1-B — Next Best Actions**: Deterministic resolver caps at 3
  actions, classified AVAILABLE_NOW / NEEDS_CONNECTION /
  NEEDS_APPROVAL. NOT_AVAILABLE never surfaces. Derives from real
  state (latest durable result, pending approvals, connected tools,
  turn-level connection suggestion). Click replays the action through
  the existing `send()` chat path — no parallel pipeline, no new
  endpoint, no new agent. Portal renders chips under the latest
  assistant reply with the existing chip surface; defensive cap at 3
  before render.

